      "writtenOn": "2025-06-10T22:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think ideally when we build the upstream tests we won\u0027t build any of our custom EC code that we have added on top. Do you know how `CONFIG_CROS_SYSTEM_NPCX` gets pulled in?\n\nI\u0027m wondering if there\u0027s a way split up our [`prj.conf`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fpmcu/helipilot/prj.conf) so that we have upstream Zephyr Kconfig settings are in one file and EC-specific ones are in another file. Then we only use the upstream version when building the upstream Zephyr tests. Would that require adding a [different \"variant\" in `BUILD.py`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fpmcu/BUILD.py;l\u003d63-66;drc\u003dd377ac3a87b2fc0e7a9460d981f1f7b7519e37bd)?",
      "range": {
