      "writtenOn": "2025-06-11T01:11:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I look at the bloonchipper upstream tests, the [CONFIG_CROS_SYSTEM_STM32](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/cros_system/Kconfig;l\u003d97?q\u003d%22config%20CROS_SYSTEM_NPCX%22\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d96-,97,-98) is not enabled because config `IWDG_STM32` is not enabled. If I delete that dependency, I will get the same error that we used to get for the helipilot upstream tests and I can see that `CONFIG_CROS_SYSTEM_STM32` is enabled.\n\nI believe we can use the same strategy for `helipilot`. We can make config [CROS_SYSTEM_NPCX](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/cros_system/Kconfig;l\u003d5?q\u003d%22config%20CROS_SYSTEM_NPCX%22\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d4-,5,-6) to depend on config [WDT_NPCX](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/drivers/watchdog/Kconfig.npcx;drc\u003dc9d8655685fbff3680c7679c47492e71801deb27;l\u003d6). The `WDT_NPCX` config is not enabled for the upstream test and will cause `CONFIG_CROS_SYSTEM_NPCX` to be disabled. It is enabled though for the `helipilot` board. I am not sure if this will have any impact on any other NPCX board and whether CQ is enough. However, I believe this is the way to go.",
      "parentUuid": "83100452_99eea7f7",
